\label{def:proper}
Let $X$ be a connected Stein manifold of dimension $>1$. 
A (possibly singular) holomorphic foliation $\mathcal{F}$ on $X$ 
is {\em proper} if every leaf $\mathcal{F}_x$ $(x\in X)$ is closed and satisfies 
$\dim \mathcal{F}_x\ge 1$, and for every compact subset $K\subset X$ the set 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:FK}
	\mathcal{F}(K) := \overline{\bigcup_{x \in K}\mathcal{F}_x} 
\end{equation} 
is such that $X\setminus \mathcal{F}(K)$ is nonempty and not relatively compact in $X$.
